  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Search First",
      "text": "[中文](./README_zh.md)\n\n**Search first, verify facts, reply last — enforced by DSH.**\n\n[](https://youtu.be/rGc5OCydHyY)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Search First",
      "text": "▶ Demo walkthrough: https://youtu.be/rGc5OCydHyY\n> A DeepSeek Harness (dsh) Cordis plugin that **forces multi-source web search before the model answers**.\n> On `agent/pre-step`, when **Search First** is enabled, \n> it runs Query Extraction → Unified Search Engine (AnySearch / TinyFish / Tavily) → fetch → organize → cache + `runs/` persistence → inject the organized live leeds guiding verification next, then returns control to the agent loop. Final answers stay with the LLM."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "1. The sub-model used for query extraction is configurable.\n2. Guides the host model to use standardized citations, as shown below.\n\n3. Models and ranks multi-source search results, and selectively fetches pages back to the host model."
    },
    {
      "section": "Installation",
      "text": "Prerequisites: a mounted `dsh` web profile (dsh ≥ 0.1.1-rc.2), Node ≥ 22.\n\n```bash"
    },
    {
      "section": "install from the GitHub repo:",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add https://github.com/v587d/dsh-search-first.git\n```\n\nUninstall: `dsh plugin --profile web remove dsh-search-first` (then restart)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Build from source",
      "text": "```bash\npnpm install\npnpm check      # vitest + typecheck (host + client)\npnpm build      # lib/ (host ESM + d.ts) + lib/client.js (browser bundle)\npnpm test"
    },
    {
      "section": "Quick start",
      "text": "> [!IMPORTANT]\n> Export at least **one** API key ([AnySearch](https://anysearch.com/) / [Tinyfish](https://www.tinyfish.ai/) / [Tavily](https://www.tavily.com/)) before running.  \n> **Free tier is ENOUGH**."
    },
    {
      "section": "Quick start",
      "text": "1. Restart `dsh web` after installing.\n2. Open Settings → **Search first** → **Search APIs** → **Test all connections**\n   (configure keys first via step 3, or the probe reports a key-missing result).\n3. Provide at least one provider key — add it to `$DSH_HOME/.credentials.yaml`\n   or `export TAVILY_API_KEY` / `ANYSEARCH_API_KEY` / `TINYFISH_API_KEY` in the\n   environment. AnySearch also works anonymously (Bearer header omitted).\n4. Back in a session, the **Search First** toggle under the input box decides\n   per session (right-click the toggle to return to the global default)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration (Settings → Search first)",
      "text": "| Section | Fields |\n|---|---|\n| General | default enabled, failure policy (`continue` / `block`), injection mode, overall timeout |\n| Query Extraction | explicit provider/model (empty = follow session model), timeout, max tokens |\n| Cache | dir (empty = `$DSH_HOME/search-first`; root applies after restart), search/fetch TTL, clear button |\n| Limits | max search results, max fetch pages, max inject chars |\n| Search APIs | mode (sequential failover / parallel fan-out + merge), big-three enable/credential-ref/priority, per-provider timeout, `ctx.web` fallback, local HTTP fallback, **Test all connections** |"
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT — see [LICENSE](./LICENSE)."
    }
  ],
